     The responsibilities of the City Clerk's office are established by City Charter and Massachusetts General Law. 
 The Clerks Office Oversees and/or Provides the Following Services: 

 Birth, Marriage, and Death records  ( long-form only, certified copies are provided ) 

 AMENDMENTS 

 Will be completed by Appointment only to ensure privacy and proper completion. 
 Can ONLY be done by either the State Division of Vital Records or by the City/Town in which: 

 Person was Born for Birth Amendment 
 Person passed away for Death Amendment 
 The City/Town where the Marriage Intention was completed. 




 CERTIFICATES for VITAL RECORDS 

 Online :  Before you place an Order, reach out to us to ensure that your document is on file in our office .

 Birth & Death Certificates are on file in the City/Town in which the person was:

 BIRTH:  Born or was a resident in when born 
 DEATH: Passed away in or was a resident when they passed away. 


 Marriage Certificates are available ONLY in the City/Town in which they filed for the Marriage Intentions 


 In Person :   Birth Certificates, Death Certificates and Marriage Certificates are ONLY available in the City/Town as listed above under online. 
 By Mail :   Please ensure first that we have your record that you wish to request.   A personal check, money order or bank check must be accompanied with the written request for the record with all information required, as well as a self addressed stamped envelope for the return of the Certificate.  


 MARRIAGE INTENTIONS 

 Will be completed by Appointment only to ensure privacy and proper completion.  




 Billiard/Poolroom License 
 Bowling Alley Licenses 
 Business Licenses (DBA) 
 Certified Copies of Cemetery Deeds 
 Census also called "Annual Street Listing"  (Annually from the City) (Every 10- Years from the Federal Government)

 If you DO NOT return your Annual City Census and are a voter, it will result in removal from the active voting list and may result in the removal from the voter registration rolls. 


 City Charter/Ordinances 
 Dog Licenses 
 Elections  -

 The City Clerk oversees each Election (Municipal; State and Federal) 
 Coverage for Elections (Poll Workers) 
 Information on and updates to each election 
 Statement of Candidates for Elections 
 Campaign Finance Reports (Local Candidates and Committees) 
 Certification of Signatures for Nominations 
 Certification of Signatures for Initiative Petitions 


 Ethics Certifications (Conflict of Interest) 


 Fuel Storage Certificates 
 Genealogy Research Due to the time required for staff to complete genealogy research, an hourly fee and per-record charge will apply.

 Please note: 

 Due to the high volume of requests, research may take  30 days or longer  to complete. 
 All requests are processed in the order they are received. 


 Our office will contact the requestor if: 

 we find there are inconsistencies between the Requestors information and what we have 
 if we require more information to complete the research for you 
 The research has been completed, to review and confirm findings  


 A completed  Genealogy Research Request Form  is required before any research can begin.

 Form:   Genealogy Research Request Form 
 Email to:  CityClerk@northadams-ma.gov 




 Notary Services 

 In accordance with Massachusetts Notarial Law, Massachusetts General Laws Chapter 222, a Notary Public will not provide service if the customer, document, or circumstances of the request for Notary service raise any issue of authenticity, ambiguity, doubt, or uncertainty.   In this event, the Notary may, at his/her sole discretion, decline to provide Notary Services. 


 Open Meeting Law Information and tracking of Acknowledgements 
 Pole Location Hearings/Orders 
 Postings for Meetings & Minutes to Boards and Website 
 Raffle & Bazaar Licenses 
 Sunday Licenses 
 Taxi Operators License & Taxi Driver Licenses 
 Transient Vendor License 
 Voter Registration, changes in Voter Registration, Absentee Voting 

